{"id":24638,"path":"/grammar-points/a2/no-longer-any-longer-anymore/","parentId":542,"order":330,"section":"grammar-points","level":"a2","depth":3,"title":"No longer, any longer, anymore","seo":{"title":"No longer, any longer, anymore - Test-English","description":"Learn the difference between 'no longer', 'any longer' and 'anymore' with our A2 grammar lesson. Clear rules, examples and exercises!","image":"/media/uploads/no-longer_any-longer_anymore_A2-grammar-1.png"},"modified":"2026-02-25T09:29:54","kind":"lesson","parts":["<h3>Exercise 1</h3> <h5>Choose ‘no longer’, ‘any longer’ or ‘anymore’ to complete the sentences below.</h5> <div data-quiz=\"873\"></div>","<h3>Exercise 2</h3> <h5>Choose ‘no longer’, ‘any longer’ or ‘anymore’ for the gaps below.</h5> <div data-quiz=\"874\"></div>","<h3>Exercise 3</h3> <h5>Rewrite these sentences, adding ‘no longer’, ‘any longer’ or ‘anymore’ in the correct place.</h5> <p><em>EXAMPLE: <span class=\"textGap\">Joe no longer believes in ghosts.</span> (Joe believes in ghosts.)</em><br> </p><div data-quiz=\"875\"></div> <p></p>"],"explanation":"<p>We use the phrases <strong>no longer</strong>, <strong>any longer</strong>, and <strong>anymore</strong> to talk about something that happened or was true in the past but doesn’t happen or isn’t true now. Although their meanings are the same, the way we use them is not. <strong>No longer</strong> is also slightly more formal than <strong>any longer</strong> and <strong>anymore</strong>.<br> <br> <img src=\"/media/uploads/No-longer_any-longer_anymore-1.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"500\" height=\"501\" class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-24630\" loading=\"lazy\"></p> <h6></h6> <h3>No longer</h3> <p>Unlike <strong>any longer</strong> and <strong>anymore</strong>, <strong>no longer</strong> is only used in positive sentences as it makes a sentence negative. Its position is different, too, as it is typically used in the <strong>mid position</strong>. The mid position is between the subject and the verb.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>I <span><strong>no longer</strong></span> eat meat.</em></li> <li><em>He <span><strong>no longer</strong></span> plays football.</em></li> </ul> <p>With the verb <a href=\"/grammar-points/a1/present-simple-forms-of-to-be/\"><strong>to be</strong></a>, however, the mid position is <strong>after the verb</strong>.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>We are <span><strong>no longer</strong></span> friends.</em></li> <li><em>He is <span><strong>no longer</strong></span> a footballer.</em></li> </ul> <p>With <a href=\"/grammar-points/a2/auxiliary-verbs-do-be-and-have/\">modal or auxiliary verbs</a>, the mid position is <strong>after the modal verb</strong>.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>Jim will <span><strong>no longer</strong></span> attend his lessons.</em></li> <li><em>We can <span><strong>no longer</strong></span> bring phones to school.</em></li> </ul> <p>In <a href=\"/grammar-points/a2/asking-questions-in-english/\">questions</a>, the mid position is <strong>after the subject</strong>.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>Do you <span><strong>no longer</strong></span> want to play?</em></li> <li><em>Is he <span><strong>no longer</strong></span> happy?</em></li> </ul> <h3>Any longer, anymore</h3> <p><strong>Any longer</strong> and <strong>anymore</strong> are only used in <strong>negative statements or questions</strong>.&nbsp;Both expressions are synonyms and can be used interchangeably. They are always placed <strong>at the end</strong> of a statement or question.<br> <br> <strong>Any longer</strong> is slightly more formal than <strong>anymore</strong>.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>We don’t live there <span><strong>any longer/anymore</strong></span>.</em></li> <li><em>We aren’t friends <span><strong>any longer/anymore</strong></span>.</em></li> <li><em>Why don’t you visit us <span><strong>any longer/anymore</strong></span>?&nbsp;</em></li> </ul> <h3>Anymore vs any more</h3> <p><strong>Anymore</strong> (one word) is often confused with <strong>any more</strong> (two words), and though the two may look similar, their meanings are completely different.<br> <br> <strong>Anymore</strong> is an adverb referring to time; it means ‘not now like before’. For example, “I don’t eat pizza anymore” means ‘I used to eat pizza in the past, but I don’t eat pizza now’.<br> <br> On the other hand, <strong>any more</strong> is a determiner used to describe quantity; it means ‘additional’ or ‘more than what we have now’. For example, “Do you have any more candy?” means ‘Do you have additional candy (or more candy than what you gave me)?’</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>I don’t eat chicken <strong><span>anymore</span></strong>. <img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21425\" src=\"/media/uploads/correct.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></em></li> <li><em>I don’t eat chicken <span><strong>any more</strong></span>. <img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21426\" src=\"/media/uploads/wrong.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></em></li> <li><em>Do you want <strong><span>any more</span></strong> chicken? <img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21425\" src=\"/media/uploads/correct.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></em></li> <li><em>Do you want <strong><span>anymore</span></strong> chicken? <img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21426\" src=\"/media/uploads/wrong.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></em></li> </ul>","quizzes":[{"id":873,"questions":[{"id":7437,"num":"1","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>We <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> work together.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["any longer","no longer","anymore"]}]},{"id":7438,"num":"2","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>John doesn’t work here <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["anymore","no longer","any more"]}]},{"id":7439,"num":"3","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Mr. Lee doesn’t teach us <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["any more","any longer","no longer"]}]},{"id":7440,"num":"4","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Why don’t you sit with us <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["anymore","no longer","any more"]}]},{"id":7441,"num":"5","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Alfred <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> goes to church.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["no longer","any longer","anymore"]}]},{"id":7442,"num":"6","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Now that I’m vegan, I <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> eat cheese.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["any longer","no longer","anymore"]}]},{"id":7443,"num":"7","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>I cannot stay here <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["any more","any longer","no longer"]}]},{"id":7444,"num":"8","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>She says she doesn’t love me <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["any more","anymore","no longer"]}]},{"id":7445,"num":"9","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>We are <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> in the same class.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["anymore","any longer","no longer"]}]},{"id":7446,"num":"10","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>I haven’t seen you together lately. Are you <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> friends?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["anymore","any longer","no longer"]}]}]},{"id":874,"questions":[{"id":7447,"num":"1","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>Jean doesn’t live here _____.</div>","choices":[{"id":13000,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>any more</span>"},{"id":13001,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>no longer</span>"},{"id":13002,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>anymore</span>"}]},{"id":7448,"num":"2","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>We _____ share a house.</div>","choices":[{"id":13003,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>no longer</span>"},{"id":13004,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>any longer</span>"},{"id":13005,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>anymore</span>"}]},{"id":7449,"num":"3","type":"checkbox","prompt":"<div>We don’t have a dog _____. <span class=\"highlighter\">Choose TWO correct answers</span></div>","maxSelections":2,"choices":[{"id":13006,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>any longer</span>"},{"id":13007,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>anymore</span>"},{"id":13008,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>no longer</span>"}]},{"id":7450,"num":"4","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>Why doesn’t he talk to us _____?</div>","choices":[{"id":13009,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>any more</span>"},{"id":13010,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>any longer</span>"},{"id":13011,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>no longer</span>"}]},{"id":7451,"num":"5","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>James _____ smokes cigarettes.</div>","choices":[{"id":13012,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>any longer</span>"},{"id":13013,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>anymore</span>"},{"id":13014,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>no longer</span>"}]},{"id":7452,"num":"6","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>We rarely see each other _____.</div>","choices":[{"id":13015,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>any more</span>"},{"id":13016,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>no longer</span>"},{"id":13017,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>anymore</span>"}]},{"id":7453,"num":"7","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>Now that we live in the countryside, we _____ worry about crime.</div>","choices":[{"id":13018,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>no longer</span>"},{"id":13019,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>anymore</span>"},{"id":13020,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>any longer</span>"}]},{"id":7454,"num":"8","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>John doesn’t have a beard _____.</div>","choices":[{"id":13021,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>any longer</span>"},{"id":13022,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>any more</span>"},{"id":13023,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>no longer</span>"}]},{"id":7455,"num":"9","type":"checkbox","prompt":"<div>Sandra doesn’t work here _____. <span class=\"highlighter\">Choose TWO correct answers</span></div>","maxSelections":2,"choices":[{"id":13024,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>anymore</span>"},{"id":13025,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>any longer</span>"},{"id":13026,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>no longer</span>"}]},{"id":7456,"num":"10","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>Now that he’s retired, Peter _____ wakes up early.</div>","choices":[{"id":13027,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>no longer</span>"},{"id":13028,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>anymore</span>"},{"id":13029,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>any longer</span>"}]}]},{"id":875,"questions":[{"id":7457,"num":"1","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p><span data-gap=\"0\"></span>. (John doesn’t live in London.)</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":7458,"num":"2","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p><span data-gap=\"0\"></span>. (Ms Peters is our teacher.)</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":7459,"num":"3","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p><span data-gap=\"0\"></span>? (Why don’t you call us?)</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":7460,"num":"4","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p><span data-gap=\"0\"></span>. (Ian belongs to the gym.)</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":7461,"num":"5","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p><span data-gap=\"0\"></span>. (We are in the same class.)</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":7462,"num":"6","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p><span data-gap=\"0\"></span>. (She doesn’t wear glasses.)</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":7463,"num":"7","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p><span data-gap=\"0\"></span>. (Robert can hear very well.)</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":7464,"num":"8","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p><span data-gap=\"0\"></span>. (Fred doesn’t like carrots.)</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":7465,"num":"9","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p><span data-gap=\"0\"></span>. (The property is for sale.)</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":7466,"num":"10","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p><span data-gap=\"0\"></span>. (We can’t wear jeans to work.)</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]}]}]}